# build outputs
target/
dist/
*.iso

# The KASLR relocation table (`src/arch/x86_64/kaslr_relocs.generated.rs`) is
# generated by `make gen-kaslr-relocs` and **tracked**: the `kaslr` build
# `include!`s it, so a clone that does not have it cannot build that
# configuration at all, and `make check-x8664-kaslr-runtime` compares a fresh
# generation against the tracked file — a gate needs something to compare
# against, and the alternative (an ignored file) has nothing.  Regenerating
# it is `make gen-kaslr-relocs`; the fixed array length is what makes one
# generation enough.

# ISO tree outputs (entirely build artifacts)
isodir/
iso/boot/*.elf
iso/boot/*.bin
iso/boot/grub/*.mod

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
